 "text": "You've heard Black Friday mean stores finally make a profit. That's not where the name came from. Back in the early 1960s in Philadelphia, the day after Thanksgiving is total chaos. Shoppers flood downtown. The Army-Navy football game is that weekend too. Traffic jams everywhere. Police officers have to work long shifts. They give the day a grumpy nickname, Black Friday. Store owners hate it. They try to rebrand it Big Friday. It doesn't stick. By the 1980s, a happier story appears. Black Friday is when stores go from red ink to black. A nice story, just not the original one. A cop's complaint that became one of America's biggest shopping days. Every legend has a beginning.",
